Z||000000||BAM-BAM||02-06-2001||08:19 PM||||   To those on the Forum who care to read this. I, as well as others, am not condeming anyone for there lack of donations to the ABF. First off, Why are people getting so defensive? If you have extinuating cicumstances, then so be it. No one is pressuring anyone to donate to this cause. The fact of the matter is; When this whole idea got started there was overwhelming support from the forum to start this fund. If there wasn't then there would have been no fund started. The tone of my reply to another post was ment as a reminder for those who jumped on the band wagon but had no showing (so far). There was no pressure on anyone to  divert their neccessary capital in this direction. If you had the change lying around and felt like you wanted to help, great! If not, great! <BR>  Now, another thing. Some on the forum are trying to make this out to be a for proffit concern.  There is no one proffiting from this in any way. Tim's idea was to break even and give all the proffits to the fund and at the same time allow you, members of the Forum, the opportunity to own a complete set of T-Tops for $50.00. That's a 1 in 60 chance. Where will you ever find those kinds of odds. You don't like it or feel offended by it? Then don't respond to it. It's that simple. <BR>  Also and in closing, no one is required to give any certain amount. If you have pocket change lying around and that's all, that's fine. It all adds up. You are free to excercise your free will, no pressure. In return you will help someone who truly "NEEDS" it and make a good name for Fiero owners every where. Go ahead and take your shots at me, I won't be responding.||||reg||1
