Z||000007||BAM-BAM||02-06-2001||09:24 PM||||  Ok, so I lied. I will respond. Let me ask you Black, Just how much do you think it cost to purchase and stock T-Top kits for the Fiero? Wait, how about this, can you even find anyone who makes the T-Top kits for Fiero's? Wait, how about this, if you had access to T-Tops, how much would it cost you to supply the various seals and weather strips involed? Wait, I'm not finished with your arrogant ass. Do you know of anyone who even manufactures the various seals and weather strips? Have you any idea what they want for such a limited production of replacement parts? When was the last time you tried to purchase a new Fiero T-Top kit? I'll guarentee you that the price is well over $3000.00. You are obviusly just looking to argue. You need to do youe home work first BOY! <BR>  Tim bought the last of the T-Top kits from C&C before they went out of buisness. If Tim hadn't bought them, no one would be getting Fiero T-Tops. Along with that he purchased all that was left of the P-seals and weather strips. Tim has inquired with the OEM of those "HARD" to find parts and was rather taken aback by there answer. You couldn't afford to even buy the seals at what they wanted.  <BR>  Tim is a buisness man who happens to deal in Fiero parts. Anyone in buisness knows that along with the inventory you have overhead, and stocking. Tim is not tying to proffit. He's taking care of buisness and at the same time, trying to be a genuine community member. You on the other hand are just trying to rock the boat. I think you should go back and read the "CLARIFICATION". If you don't like it or agree with it, then don't endulge it. And certainly do not try to squash the mans generosity. <P>  OUT!!!  <p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||1
