Z||000023||JohnnyK||02-07-2001||01:22 PM||||I just don't like the idea that Anthony Barber is getting all this special treatment. I mean, I AM glad, I just think it is highly uncalled for. He lived, he's doing fine. What about the other person that was killed?? What about the hundreds of other people that are killed or seriously maimed? Hell, your going to give and give to someone because they drove a car that you liked? If I had excess money, I would give to a charity (not necessarily this one, but some). I'm not saying you guys are wrong for doing this, I just think that you misplaced your efforts.  Think of how the family of the deceased would feel if they knew about this and were getting ignored just because no one favoured the car he was driving.  Sorry, had to get this off my chest.<BR>And Fieroparts.com, if you want to cancel somebodies order because you don't like them, fine, but don't expect to get much business from many people.  "Oh my god, I said something he didn't like, am I going to get what I ordered??". Yeah, I want that running through my head all day.||||reg||1
Z||000024||fieroparts.com||02-07-2001||02:03 PM||||You can not read! <BR>I never said I paid $2000.00<BR>for a kit. I said it cost $2000.00 to put a kit together after the fact.<BR>And for yout information back in 1995<BR>Rob Allen and I put a deal together<BR>with Phil Edwards (at that time in charge<BR>of C&C) for two complete kits for $3,000.00<BR>and the kits did not include the roof frame<BR>or the header bar.  I also (from mrfiero two years ago) pick up a new roof and misc. trim<BR>for $1,000.00 to complete a kit. Some kits<BR>end up costing more, some less.<BR>Let me do the math for you on that one,<BR>SO THE TOTAL FOR THAT KIT IS $2,500.00<BR>so the next one might come in at $1,500.00.<BR>so I hope you can now see that I would only be getting my money back.<P>Remember you started this crap!<BR>no one wants to here your neg. bullshit!<P>SOME PEOPLE!<P>Let's move on and see if we can help someone in  need!<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Well, as much as I would love to make a similar grade school comeback as Tim has, I will regretfully decline.<P>The fact of the matter is, you are getting rid of a t-top kit, and keeping $2,000.  If thats not profit I don't know what is.  I find it hard to believe that you bought the t-top kit from C&C for $2,000.  This is coming from someone advertises USED spark plug wires for 150 bucks.  Give me a break.  <P>[b]The number of ticket sales speaks for itself...</B>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||jlruiz67||02-07-2001||11:57 PM||||Well, I'm considered a very positive person but I must admit that Black88GT has a point. Fieroparts.com is not showing much generosity, as for profits, I can see how one would question your numbers. $2,000.00 is a lot of money and if your not making a profit, there must be something wrong on how you run your business. I don't understand how  you get off as a business talking all that trash. I also don't understand how you can threaten some one with canceling there  back orders. It seems that your to defensive on this issue and it makes me question your motives. You can now call me names and get all worked up, I do not have any backorders with you and have never done business with you ( not that I wouldn't if I needed a product or service you provided ).<P>I noticed that there seems to be a case of worshiping of parts suppliers on this forum, it should be the other way around, without us, the Fiero owner, all the suppliers would be out of business. Excuse me but if you are in business you are there to serve your clientele not the other way around. I feels like if we pissed you off or question you, we would be punished by you not selling us parts. Isn't this ridiculous. Some might say that if it was not for them we would not be able to buy parts for our great cars, for you I have to say, remember supply and demand. If you have demand there will be supply, not the other way around.<P><BR>people give me a break, If you are going to be part of a charity I would expect you to donate a product, they way it is now, the people in this forum will buy a product from the fieroparts.com for the high price of $3,000.00 then for that privilege the fieroparts.com will then send $1,000.00 of the PROFITS and then KEEP the rest. I personally don't have a problem with that but don't try to come out as some great humanitarian and get pissed when someone questions  your motives.<P>I'm sure that someone will let me have it now. I will not respond to any negative comments because I don't have to.||||reg||1
